  "id": "COMPOUND:29473 - PROTEIN:5940",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol and Carboxylesterase 2, mediated through the cell line Raji and other compounds. The drug (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol is identified as a target of Raji, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside and a complex metabolite. These compounds are all linked to Carboxylesterase 2, indicating a possible mechanism of action where (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol may interact with Carboxylesterase 2 through a shared target, Raji, or through a direct interaction with the enzyme. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, suggesting a possible dependency on the enzyme for the activity of the compounds, and the presence of multiple pathways pointing to Carboxylesterase 2 as a target. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol may exert its effects by modulating Carboxylesterase 2, possibly through a direct or indirect interaction.",
